draft: true
id: E3141
title: Conan test_package must select the host executable suffix explicitly
scope: conan test_package cmake windows ohos cross-build executable suffix self.run
symptoms: A CMake Conan test_package links its consumer successfully but test() reports the executable is missing on Windows because the recipe searches for a suffix-less name while the host linker emitted .exe.
root_cause: Conan's bindir points to the build output, but executable naming is host-platform specific. Windows emits test_eigen.exe while an OHOS ELF target is conventionally suffix-less; assuming one spelling makes the runtime gate fail after a valid build.
repair: Derive the binary name from the Conan host OS, check the resulting regular file in the bound bindir, and keep explicit self.run(binary, env="conanrun"). Use can_run(self) for cross-builds so host execution is skipped without being reported as target PASS.
verification: Eigen 5.0.1 conan create first reproduced the missing test_eigen failure, then the host-OS suffix fix produced test_eigen.exe and the consumer printed "eigen smoke test: PASS (matmul + norm OK)" with RC 0. The same rule preserves the suffix-less OHOS name for the device path.
boundaries: This only closes executable discovery for Conan consumers. It does not prove dynamic-loader setup, signing, OHOS execution, upstream CTest coverage, or W3; those require their own same-snapshot evidence.
evidence: F:\\HarmonyPC\\eigen-5.0.1-adapt-20260908\\evidence\\conan-create.log; F:\\HarmonyPC\\eigen-5.0.1-adapt-20260908\\evidence\\conan-create-rerun.log
